Usage: vmstat [OPTION]...

Report virtual memory statistics.
On Windows, reports memory, swap, and CPU utilization.

OPTIONS:
  -a, --active     split into active and inactive memory
  -d               show memory statistics
  -f, --forks      show boot/forks counts
  -n, --oneline    print headings only once
  -p, --pid ARG    show statistics for a specific PID
  -s, --summary    print summary information only
  -t, --timestamp  include timestamp
  -w, --wide       wide output
  -m, --slab       show slab information (not supported on Windows)
  -v, --version    print version and exit
      --help       display this help and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
